      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To determine the effects of SGB in BCRL patients and the efficacy of corticosteroids in SGB."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "STUDY DESIGN",
          "content": "A double-blinded, randomized, controlled trial."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "SETTING",
          "content": "A single academic hospital, outpatient setting."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "In total, 32 patients with BCRL were recruited. Patients were divided randomly into 3 groups (Group A: 0.5% bupivacaine 5 mL, n = 12; Group B: 0.5% bupivacaine 4.5 mL + 20 mg of triamcinolone 0.5 mL, n = 10; and Group C: 0.5% bupivacaine 4 mL + 40 mg of triamcinolone 1 mL, n = 10). All patients received 3 consecutive SGBs, every 2 weeks. The primary outcomes were changes in forearm and upper arm circumference. Circumference was measured at baseline, 2 weeks (before the second injection), 4 weeks (before the third injection), and 8 weeks (one month follow-up after 3 consecutive SGBs). Moreover, subjective data were collected using EORTC C-30 at baseline and 8 weeks."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "After 3 consecutive SGBs, forearm and upper arm circumferences were decreased significantly from baseline in all groups (P < 0.05/3). The upper arm circumference of group C was reduced significantly more than that of group A (P < 0.05/3). The subjective data by EORTC-C30 at baseline and one month after 3 consecutive SGBs revealed no statistically significant difference."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "LIMITATIONS",
          "content": "Relatively few patients were enrolled. We did not compare SGB with any other BCRL treatment, such as complex decongestive therapy."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "This study suggests that SGB may be an effective treatment for BCRL. Furthermore, it appears that corticosteroids could have an additive effect in SGB."
        }
      ]},
